  "summary": "Discord token stealer exfiltrating to hardcoded webhook",
  "details": "pylever 1.0.11 harvests Discord authentication credentials from the installer's machine and sends them to an attacker-controlled Discord webhook. On execution the package recursively scans Path.home() and the roots of C:/, D:/, and E:/ for tokens.txt files; reads Chrome, Edge, and Brave 'User Data' LevelDB and Cache stores under AppData/Local; and reads the Discord desktop app's LevelDB and Cache under AppData/Roaming/discord. Extracted strings matching the Discord token regex (MTA[A-Za-z0-9_-]{69}) and MFA regex (mfa\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{84}) are validated against discord.com/api/v10/users/@me, and each valid token together with the associated account metadata (username, id, email, verified, bot flag) is POSTed as JSON to the hardcoded webhook https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1547416857537945601/.... The 'Credential Manager' naming does not correspond to any legitimate credential-management behavior; the code is a targeted Discord account stealer.",
